{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Atev5UnqVi9JtsuXxdsqBL","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CVPR 2026 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://cvpr.thecvf.com/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuidelinesq\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers\",\"url\":\"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about CoRL 2026, though specific details about the 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form are limited in the results. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Overview\n\nCoRL 2026 will be held November 9-12, 2026 in Austin, Texas, US.\n\n## Reviewer Requirements\n\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer. They are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal.\n\n## Review Process\n\nThe search results included more detailed information from previous CoRL conferences. For instance, review criteria include evaluating whether the paper addresses a problem in robot learning, applies or improves a learning-based method, evaluates the method in simulation, on real robots, or both, and whether the CoRL audience will be interested.\n\nHowever, the specific 2026 reviewer guidelines document and detailed review form information don't appear to be fully available in these search results yet. You may want to check the official CoRL 2026 website (corl.org) or the OpenReview page for the most current and complete reviewer guidelines and review form details.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"93674eff-e87d-408e-ae27-8e2925426350","uuid":"abca3e2f-d145-42f1-8c44-3072a2e47794","timestamp":"2026-05-16T08:42:36.693Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_016EG4BcuF2BY3X6JXimBFUu","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2026","url":"https://www.corl.org/"},{"title":"Robot Learning Foundation","url":"https://www.robot-learning.org/"},{"title":"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"CVPR 2026 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://cvpr.thecvf.com/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuidelinesq"},{"title":"Instructions for Reviewers","url":"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about CoRL 2026, though specific details about the 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form are limited in the results. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Overview\n\nCoRL 2026 will be held November 9-12, 2026 in Austin, Texas, US.\n\n## Reviewer Requirements\n\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer. They are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal.\n\n## Review Process\n\nThe search results included more detailed information from previous CoRL conferences. For instance, review criteria include evaluating whether the paper addresses a problem in robot learning, applies or improves a learning-based method, evaluates the method in simulation, on real robots, or both, and whether the CoRL audience will be interested.\n\nHowever, the specific 2026 reviewer guidelines document and detailed review form information don't appear to be fully available in these search results yet. You may want to check the official CoRL 2026 website (corl.org) or the OpenReview page for the most current and complete reviewer guidelines and review form details."],"durationSeconds":5.578887546999998}}
