{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UGBwwkLjkGKxdKx1a9P5F2","type":"tool_result","content":"# CoRL 2024 Review Form Analysis\n\nBased on the provided webpage content, I cannot extract a complete review form with specific rating scales or numerical scoring rubrics. The document provided contains only **review criteria and desk rejection guidelines**, not the actual review form itself.\n\n## Available Information:\n\n**Review Criteria for Regular Papers:**\n- Evaluation focuses on \"significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical\"\n- Assessment includes \"degree to which they have been objectively established and/or their potential for scientific and technological impact\"\n- Relevance to robotic learning is required\n\n**Desk Rejection Criteria:**\nThe document specifies three grounds for desk rejection:\n1. Formatting issues (length or format violations)\n2. Anonymity violations\n3. Scope issues (must demonstrate robot learning relevance through intent or outcome)\n\n## Missing Elements:\n\nThe webpage does not provide:\n- Numerical rating scales\n- Specific score definitions (e.g., 1-5 or 1-10)\n- Detailed review form questions\n- Scoring rubrics for different evaluation dimensions\n\n**Note:** To obtain the complete review form with rating scales, you would need to access the actual submission portal or contact the CoRL 2024 organizing committee directly."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"93674eff-e87d-408e-ae27-8e2925426350","uuid":"48d1565e-2989-4d89-baf1-df313b48accf","timestamp":"2026-05-16T08:43:01.953Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":134029,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# CoRL 2024 Review Form Analysis\n\nBased on the provided webpage content, I cannot extract a complete review form with specific rating scales or numerical scoring rubrics. The document provided contains only **review criteria and desk rejection guidelines**, not the actual review form itself.\n\n## Available Information:\n\n**Review Criteria for Regular Papers:**\n- Evaluation focuses on \"significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical\"\n- Assessment includes \"degree to which they have been objectively established and/or their potential for scientific and technological impact\"\n- Relevance to robotic learning is required\n\n**Desk Rejection Criteria:**\nThe document specifies three grounds for desk rejection:\n1. Formatting issues (length or format violations)\n2. Anonymity violations\n3. Scope issues (must demonstrate robot learning relevance through intent or outcome)\n\n## Missing Elements:\n\nThe webpage does not provide:\n- Numerical rating scales\n- Specific score definitions (e.g., 1-5 or 1-10)\n- Detailed review form questions\n- Scoring rubrics for different evaluation dimensions\n\n**Note:** To obtain the complete review form with rating scales, you would need to access the actual submission portal or contact the CoRL 2024 organizing committee directly.","durationMs":3714,"url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JxmSNMiaJpRG9oHMwMUJyT","type":"tool_result","content":"# CoRL 2023 Reviewer Guidelines Summary\n\n## Review Form Fields\n\nThe guidelines specify these evaluation dimensions:\n\n1. **Summary of Paper** - Restate contributions in your own words rather than copying the abstract\n2. **Main Review** - Evaluate across six dimensions:\n   - Originality\n   - Quality\n   - Clarity\n   - Significance\n   - Relevance\n   - Limitations\n\n## Evaluation Dimensions\n\n**Originality:** \"Are the problems or methods new? Is the work a novel combination of well-known techniques?\"\n\n**Quality:** \"Is the submission technically sound? Are claims well supported (e.g., by theoretical analysis or experimental results)?\"\n\n**Clarity:** \"Is the submission clearly written? Is it well organized?\"\n\n**Significance:** \"Are the results important? Are others (researchers or practitioners) likely to use the ideas or build on them?\"\n\n**Relevance:** \"Does the paper address a problem in robot learning? Does it apply or improve a learning-based method?\"\n\n**Limitations:** CoRL requires papers include limitations sections; \"treat the honestly reported limitations kindly.\"\n\n## Numerical Scores & Rubric\n\n**The document does not specify numerical rating scales, point systems, or numerical scoring criteria.** It provides qualitative guidance on evaluation dimensions but omits the actual scoring rubric, point ranges, or their numerical meanings that would appear on the actual review form.\n\nThe guidelines emphasize constructive feedback and avoiding common reviewer mistakes rather than detailing scoring mechanics."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"93674eff-e87d-408e-ae27-8e2925426350","uuid":"e3ce7589-d505-4c55-8d6d-941fe0f04e99","timestamp":"2026-05-16T08:43:03.538Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":105095,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# CoRL 2023 Reviewer Guidelines Summary\n\n## Review Form Fields\n\nThe guidelines specify these evaluation dimensions:\n\n1. **Summary of Paper** - Restate contributions in your own words rather than copying the abstract\n2. **Main Review** - Evaluate across six dimensions:\n   - Originality\n   - Quality\n   - Clarity\n   - Significance\n   - Relevance\n   - Limitations\n\n## Evaluation Dimensions\n\n**Originality:** \"Are the problems or methods new? Is the work a novel combination of well-known techniques?\"\n\n**Quality:** \"Is the submission technically sound? Are claims well supported (e.g., by theoretical analysis or experimental results)?\"\n\n**Clarity:** \"Is the submission clearly written? Is it well organized?\"\n\n**Significance:** \"Are the results important? Are others (researchers or practitioners) likely to use the ideas or build on them?\"\n\n**Relevance:** \"Does the paper address a problem in robot learning? Does it apply or improve a learning-based method?\"\n\n**Limitations:** CoRL requires papers include limitations sections; \"treat the honestly reported limitations kindly.\"\n\n## Numerical Scores & Rubric\n\n**The document does not specify numerical rating scales, point systems, or numerical scoring criteria.** It provides qualitative guidance on evaluation dimensions but omits the actual scoring rubric, point ranges, or their numerical meanings that would appear on the actual review form.\n\nThe guidelines emphasize constructive feedback and avoiding common reviewer mistakes rather than detailing scoring mechanics.","durationMs":6241,"url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"}}
