{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PVgfXkUVgDtcQUd6HZBT5k","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL openreview review form \"overall score\" \"1:\" \"2:\" \"3:\" accept reject\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Default Review Form | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://docs.openreview.net/reference/default-forms/default-review-form\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"2024 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2024/ReviewerGuidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Frequently Asked Questions\",\"url\":\"https://corl2022.org/frequently-asked-questions/\"},{\"title\":\"2025 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2023-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2025-paper-list/\"},{\"title\":\"A simple Training-Free Method for Rejection Option | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=K1DdnjL6p7\"},{\"title\":\"Under review as a conference paper at ICLR 2021 AN OPEN REVIEW OF OPENREVIEW:\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/pdf?id=Cn706AbJaKW\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about OpenReview's default review form, but the results don't contain the specific CoRL review form with the exact format you're looking for. However, I can provide some relevant information:\n\nThe OpenReview default review form includes a rating field with options: \"10: Top 5% of accepted papers, seminal paper\", \"9: Top 15% of accepted papers, strong accept\", \"8: Top 50% of accepted papers, clear accept\", \"7: Good paper, accept\", \"6: Marginally above acceptance threshold\", \"5: Marginally below acceptance threshold\", \"4: Ok but not good enough - rejection\", \"3: Clear rejection\", \"2: Strong rejection\", \"1: Trivial or wrong\".\n\nThe search results also show references to CoRL's review process. Papers that receive all reviews in the \"reject\" range in the initial round will not proceed to the rebuttal phase.\n\nHowever, the specific CoRL OpenReview review form with the exact formatting you mentioned (with \"1:\", \"2:\", \"3:\" score labels and the particular structure you're asking about) is not explicitly shown in these search results. If you need to access the actual CoRL review form, you may want to check the CoRL OpenReview conference page directly or contact the conference organizers.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"93674eff-e87d-408e-ae27-8e2925426350","uuid":"f5063eee-a061-45ba-8606-c9156a4a954b","timestamp":"2026-05-16T08:43:12.098Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL openreview review form \"overall score\" \"1:\" \"2:\" \"3:\" accept reject","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01CXe3qdsVonBxnKDHcU8JFY","content":[{"title":"Default Review Form | OpenReview","url":"https://docs.openreview.net/reference/default-forms/default-review-form"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"2024 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2024/ReviewerGuidelines"},{"title":"Frequently Asked Questions","url":"https://corl2022.org/frequently-asked-questions/"},{"title":"2025 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2023 Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2023-statistics/"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2025-paper-list/"},{"title":"A simple Training-Free Method for Rejection Option | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/forum?id=K1DdnjL6p7"},{"title":"Under review as a conference paper at ICLR 2021 AN OPEN REVIEW OF OPENREVIEW:","url":"https://openreview.net/pdf?id=Cn706AbJaKW"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about OpenReview's default review form, but the results don't contain the specific CoRL review form with the exact format you're looking for. However, I can provide some relevant information:\n\nThe OpenReview default review form includes a rating field with options: \"10: Top 5% of accepted papers, seminal paper\", \"9: Top 15% of accepted papers, strong accept\", \"8: Top 50% of accepted papers, clear accept\", \"7: Good paper, accept\", \"6: Marginally above acceptance threshold\", \"5: Marginally below acceptance threshold\", \"4: Ok but not good enough - rejection\", \"3: Clear rejection\", \"2: Strong rejection\", \"1: Trivial or wrong\".\n\nThe search results also show references to CoRL's review process. Papers that receive all reviews in the \"reject\" range in the initial round will not proceed to the rebuttal phase.\n\nHowever, the specific CoRL OpenReview review form with the exact formatting you mentioned (with \"1:\", \"2:\", \"3:\" score labels and the particular structure you're asking about) is not explicitly shown in these search results. If you need to access the actual CoRL review form, you may want to check the CoRL OpenReview conference page directly or contact the conference organizers."],"durationSeconds":5.1850975330000075}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01MWXSVDRuUoXZdW1jK7cC1H","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, I now have enough information. The OpenReview default review form uses a 1-10 scale. CoRL uses OpenReview. Let me also check CoRL acceptance rates.\n\nBased on my research:\n- CoRL uses OpenReview\n- The standard OpenReview rating scale is 1-10\n- CoRL 2023/2024 acceptance rate is around 30-35%\n- Review dimensions: Originality, Quality, Clarity, Significance, Relevance, Limitations\n\nLet me now construct the review. I need to:\n1. Dispatch two reviewers (R1: methods+experiments, R2: novelty+related work) \n\n\n2. Run the full roundtable\n\nI'll structure this as R1 focusing on methods and experiments while R2 covers novelty and related work, then proceed through the 4-step roundtable discussion. Now I'm ready to write the actual review. The paper presents IMM (Importance Margin Maximization) for robust VLA token compression—the core contribution is maximizing the importance margin between retained and pruned tokens to improve stability under adversarial perturbations, with a formal bound, ACIS module, and two-stage training approach.\n\nLooking at the results, LIBERO-Plus shows 54.4% success rate compared to 31.9% for compression-only, with 87% token preservation versus 32%. However, the imagined experiments reveal some concerning patterns: there's a 10 percentage point success rate drop on aloha_sim_insertion, the G3 metric exceeds 1.0 on LIBERO (ranging 1.12-1.25) which contradicts the \"denoising\" claim, and the theoretical bound is quite loose at 3-19x. The token importance analysis is also problematic—pruned tokens don't clearly separate as noise with an attention weight ratio of only 0.69 and marginal statistical significance (p=0.08). Performance degrades significantly on OpenVLA where the margin ratio drops to 12.5x compared to 93.2x for SmolVLA, and across external methods, all +IMM variants show G3 > 1.0.\n\nNow I'm writing the full review and dispatching R1.\n\nI'll run both reviewers in parallel and then synthesize their findings in the roundtable discussion. Let me also reference the CoRL rating scale to calibrate my assessment properly.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1113,"cache_read_input_tokens":67742,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1113},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"93674eff-e87d-408e-ae27-8e2925426350","uuid":"fe0897a0-920d-4036-904e-1e415d00cf6c"}
