·ReLU(W1·CrossAttn(q_action, vi)))\n- Margin loss: L_margin = max(0, α − (s(k) − s(k+1)))\n- Two-stage: Stage 1 freeze backbone, train ACIS with L_margin; Stage 2 freeze ACIS, LoRA fine-tune backbone\n- Joint training G3=3.19×, grad-isolated G3=1.34×, two-stage G3=0.87× (aloha only)\n\n### Experimental Results\n\n**Table 1 (LIBERO-Plus 7-dim perturbation, headline):**\n- No compress avg SR: 67.1%, Compress-only: 31.9%, IMM+Compress: 54.4%, Preservation: 86.6%\n- Recovery = 64% of compression-induced loss\n- Perturbation dims: camera pose, lighting, texture, distractor, background, table/object color\n\n**Table 2 (aloha_sim_insertion, 50 episodes):**\n- Baseline: 78% SR, v8b+ACIS prune 50%: 68% SR (-10pp), bypass: 42%, random prune: 35%\n- Action loss: baseline 0.00406, v8b+prune 0.00354 (lower loss but lower SR — nonlinear)\n\n**Table 3 (LIBERO cross-task):**\n- Object: 72→61% (-11pp, G3=1.18), Spatial: 65→58% (-7pp, G3=1.12), Goal: 58→48% (-10pp, G3=1.25)\n- All G3>1.0. Preservation: 85-91%, avg 88%\n\n**Table 4 (Cross-model):**\n- SmolVLA 2B: G3=1.18, margin 93.2×, pres +54pp, SR -9.3pp\n- OpenVLA 7B: G3=1.28, margin 12.5×, pres +55pp, SR -13pp\n- Margin ratio drops 7.5× from 2B to 7B\n\n**Table 5 (Cross-compression plug-in):**\n- FastV: pres 32→84%, G3 1.05→1.22 (+0.17)\n- VLA-IAP: pres 29→81%, G3 1.08→1.30 (+0.22)\n- VLA-Cache: pres 35→87%, G3 1.02→1.18 (+0.16)\n- ACIS: pres 34→89%, G3 1.00→0.87 (-0.13) — only G3<1.0, aloha-specific\n\n**Table 6 (Defense comparison):**\n- No defense: pres 0.34, SR 0\n- Adversarial training: pres 0.52, SR -18pp, 3.2× train\n- Rand. smoothing: pres 0.61, SR -22pp, 8× infer\n- Jacobian reg: pres 0.48, SR -12pp, 2.1× train\n- IMM: pres 0.88, SR -9.3pp, 1.35× train, 1× infer — dominates\n\n**Table 7 (Bound verification):**\n- ε=0.01: theoretical 0.076, empirical 0.008, tightness 9.5×\n- ε=0.1: theoretical 0.76, empirical 0.245, tightness 3.1×\n- Baseline at ε=0.01: theoretical >1.0 (vacuous), empirical 0.665; IMM 83× better\n\n**Table 9 (Pruning ratio sweep, aloha):**\n- U-shaped G3 curve, min at k=0.6 (G3=0.82)\n- k=0.5: G3=0.87, k=0.3: G3=1.42, k=0.9: G3=0.96\n\n**Table 10 (Training mode ablation):**\n- Joint: G3=3.19, margin 64.3×, backbone damage\n- Grad-isolated: G3=1.34, margin 50.2×, implicit drift\n- Two-stage: G3=0.87, margin 93.2×, preserved\n\n**Table 11 (Annealing):** Fixed k=0.5 (G3=0.87) vs anneal 0.9→0.5 (G3=0.91) — annealing not beneficial\n\n**Table 12 (Token importance):**\n- Attn weight ratio pruned/retained: 0.69 (KS p=0.08, not significant)\n- Action gradient norm ratio: 0.43 (p=0.002, significant)\n- Pruned tokens are NOT \"noise\" in attention sense\n\n**Table 13 (Overhead):**\n- ACIS: +0.14% params, +2% latency, but with pruning: -27.4% latency, -28% memory\n\n## Experiment Design Reference (what was planned but may not all appear in paper)\n12 experiments were planned. The paper covers all 12 in tables 1-13. Key concern areas from the experiment design:\n- G3<1.0 is aloha-specific, not generalizable (LIBERO all G3>1.0)\n- Bound tightness ratio at ε=0.01 is 9.5-19× (loose)\n- Token analysis shows pruned tokens are not clearly \"noise\" (attn weight overlap 72%)\n- Margin ratio drops 7.5× from 2B to 7B model\n- ACIS is hard dependency (bypass SR drops 26pp)\n\n## Your Task\nProvide a thorough review focusing on:\n1. **Methodological soundness**: Is the formal bound correct? Is the margin loss well-motivated? Is ACIS design justified? Is two-stage training well-ablated?\n2. **Experimental rigor**: Are experiments sufficient for claims? Statistical significance? Enough episodes? Fair baselines? Are negative results honestly reported?\n3. **Reproducibility**: Are details sufficient?\n4. **Weaknesses in method/experiments**: What gaps or issues exist?\n\nOutput format:\n```\n## R1 Review: Methods and Experiments\n\n### Summary (2-3 sentences)\n\n### Strengths (bulleted)\n\n### Weaknesses (bulleted)\n\n### Questions for Authors\n\n### Missing Experiments or Analysis\n\n### Scores\n- Soundness: X/4\n- Empirical Rigor: X/4  \n- Clarity (method/experiments): X/4\n- Overall Score: X/10\n- Confidence: X/5\n```\n","uuid":"c9257a9a-862e-404a-8533-fbb31c258341","session_id":"93674eff-e87d-408e-ae27-8e2925426350"}
